# Copy to deploy/.env (never commit it) and fill in. Read by docker compose and the Slider container.
# Full list and explanations: docs/self-hosting.md

# ── Required ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public host name; DNS must point at this server. Slider runs at https://${SLIDER_DOMAIN}.
SLIDER_DOMAIN=slider.example.com
# openssl rand -hex 24   (hex only: it ends up inside DATABASE_URL)
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# Everything below is optional. Login, mail and sign-up can also be set up in the browser: after
# the first start, `docker compose logs slider` shows the link https://<SLIDER_DOMAIN>/einrichtung#token=…
# Values set here win and appear read-only on that page.

# Generated into the data volume on the first start when empty. Only set it to pin a value
# (openssl rand -base64 48; ≥ 32 characters; signs sessions, encrypts tokens and settings).
# SLIDER_SECRET=

# Behind Cloudflare (orange cloud): trust its edge addresses so rate limits see the visitor.
# Current list: https://www.cloudflare.com/ips/ – leave empty without Cloudflare.
# TRUSTED_PROXIES=173.245.48.0/20 103.21.244.0/22 103.22.200.0/22 103.31.4.0/22 141.101.64.0/18 108.162.192.0/18 190.93.240.0/20 188.114.96.0/20 197.234.240.0/22 198.41.128.0/17 162.158.0.0/15 104.16.0.0/13 104.24.0.0/14 172.64.0.0/13 131.0.72.0/22 2400:cb00::/32 2606:4700::/32 2803:f800::/32 2405:b500::/32 2405:8100::/32 2a06:98c0::/29 2c0f:f248::/32

# ── Sign-up ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# open = anyone who can sign in (default; the first login creates the account)
# invite = only invited people · domains = anyone from SIGNUP_DOMAINS
# SIGNUP=open
# SIGNUP_DOMAINS=firma.de,firma.com
# Your own address: only it may create the first account (instance admin). Comma-separated.
# BOOTSTRAP_EMAIL=

# ── Plans ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Free plan per organisation: 5 people, 3 decks. 0 = unlimited (your server, your rules).
# PLAN_FREE_MAX_MEMBERS=5
# PLAN_FREE_MAX_DECKS=3

# ── Login (or on the setup page) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Microsoft (Entra app registration; redirect URI https://<SLIDER_DOMAIN>/api/auth/microsoft/callback)
# MS_CLIENT_ID=
# MS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# MS_TENANT=common

# Google (redirect URI https://<SLIDER_DOMAIN>/api/auth/google/callback; docs/self-hosting.md)
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# OIDC, e.g. Authentik (redirect URI https://<SLIDER_DOMAIN>/api/auth/oidc/callback)
# OIDC_ISSUER=https://auth.example.com/application/o/slider/
# OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# OIDC_LABEL=Weiter mit Firmen-Login

# E-mail (login link + code, invitations), e.g. Resend: smtps://resend:<API_KEY>@smtp.resend.com:465
# SMTP_URL=smtps://user:password@smtp.example.com:465
# MAIL_FROM=Slider <slider@example.com>

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Several apps on this server: use the shared Caddy of deploy/proxy instead of Slider's own
# (docs/self-hosting.md → "Mehrere Apps auf einem Server").
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:docker-compose.shared-proxy.yml
# Only when Authentik runs through this Caddy (deploy/authentik).
# AUTHENTIK_DOMAIN=auth.example.com
# Image to run. Default: the published ghcr.io/root-bert/slider:edge (main); pin a release, e.g.
# ghcr.io/root-bert/slider:1. To build this checkout instead: SLIDER_IMAGE=slider:local and
# `docker compose up -d --build`.
# SLIDER_IMAGE=ghcr.io/root-bert/slider:1
SYNC_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=120000
SYNC_DEBOUNCE_MS=60000
